WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:05.120
What is Twinmotion and who is it for?

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.019
Great question.

3
00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:10.800
It's actually a very easy to use real time environment

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.339
in which you can use a tool to create your ideas

5
00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:16.379
and communicate those quickly

6
00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.370
and iterate them through various clients.

7
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.910
Now it gives the user the ability

8
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.089
to quickly and easily build your scenes

9
00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:25.690
and what I referred to earlier

10
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.350
as a WYSIWYG type environment

11
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.050
in which you can drag and drop

12
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.820
directly into your scene, affecting it immediately.

13
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.979
Lots of other great tools exist within Twinmotion

14
00:00:35.979 --> 00:00:38.460
but we won't be going over those today.

15
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.340
However, what we will be giving you

16
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.219
as a great overview of what you can do

17
00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:45.500
and get you started so you can take off

18
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.060
and really learn it.

19
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.240
So who is it for exactly?

20
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.899
Well, originally Twinmotion was designed

21
00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:56.219
for architect in mind only.

22
00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:58.240
However, it has branched off as you can see

23
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.920
from AEC, automotive, media and entertainment,

24
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.219
products and retail, as well as fashion.

25
00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:09.379
So it's just not for AEC anymore.
